course: dictionary
lesson: 9609
title: Stripe: a long thin line
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A stripe is a long, thin line of colour. Zebras have stripes, and so do many flags. «The Ukrainian constitution describes the flag as two equal stripes, blue above and yellow below.» Here the stripes are the two bands of colour that make up the flag.
explain: Look at the words around stripe to find its meaning. «The Zebra and the Giraffe step into the striped and blotchy shadows.» Blotchy means spotty and uneven, so striped must mean something different: lines, not spots. Stripes can also be a sign on a uniform that shows a person's rank.
explain: Stripes often repeat, so you can count them. Test your meaning by swapping in a simple word: «two equal lines, blue above and yellow below» still makes sense, so line is a good clue for stripe.
fact: A stripe is a long, thin line of colour.
fact: Stripe is a noun, and you can count stripes: one stripe, two stripes, many stripes.
fact: «Its orange stripes seem to glow like flames in the dark forest.»
fact: Stripes can help animals hide. This is called camouflage, and zebras and tigers use it.
fact: The quagga was a zebra striped only at the front, and it died out in 1883.
exercise: «The Ukrainian constitution describes the flag as two equal stripes, blue above and yellow below.» How many stripes does this flag have? | One | *Two | Four | Three
exercise: «The thylacine was a striped meat-eating marsupial that looked like a dog.» What does striped mean here? | Having no colour at all | Very fast | Having spots all over | *Having long thin lines of colour
exercise: Why do zebras have stripes? | *To help them hide, which is called camouflage | To make them look like flags | To make them faster at running | To show their rank
test: Which is a stripe? | *A long thin line of colour | A round spot of colour | A loud sound | A tall tree
test: Ella says a stripe on a uniform shows a person's what? | Height | Name | *Rank | Lunch
exam: Which best describes a stripe? | A loud sound | *A long thin line of colour | A very old castle | A round dot of colour
